## Installation

Install {{ package_name }} globally. The script requires Python 3.11 or later to be
installed, creates the virtual environment and registers the `wex` command:

```bash
sudo bash {{ path("bin/install") }}
```

To work on {{ package_name }} itself, overlay the local sources in editable mode. This
keeps the existing virtual environment, ensures the requirements.txt dependencies are
present, and installs local packages in editable mode without pulling additional
third-party dependencies:

```bash
bash {{ path("bin/install-dev") }}
```

To remove it:

```bash
sudo bash {{ path("bin/uninstall") }}
```

## Check Installation

Test if the core command works using these methods:

```bash
# Once installed globally
wex hi  # Returns "hi!"

# From wex directory (no global install required)
bash {{ path("bin/wex") }} hi  # Returns "hi!"
```
